CrossMono third-party notices
=============================

CrossMono is firmware for the M5Stack PaperMono and PaperMono-Lite, built on
CrossPoint Reader and the FreeInk SDK. This file lists the third-party code,
fonts and data in the CrossMono firmware image and in this repository, with
their licences and where to find each licence text. Each release also has the
asset crossmono-<version>-LICENSE.txt, which holds this file and the full text
of every licence named here (section 2).

Checked for CrossMono 0.1.0: CrossPoint base 2.0.0 (42d58daa), FreeInk SDK
5e94fe7, platform pioarduino 55.03.311, build environment papermono-gh_release.
Paths are relative to the repository root. Paths under .pio/libdeps/ exist
after a build; the libraries come from the sources named in platformio.ini.

These notices do not change any licence and do not grant extra permissions.


1. Licence of the firmware image
--------------------------------

CrossPoint's code and CrossMono's own code are under the MIT licence in
LICENSE. Third-party code, fonts and data keep their own licences (below).

The firmware image includes wolfSSL, which is licensed under the GNU GPL
version 2 or, at your option, any later version. The combined firmware image
is therefore distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
(text: licenses/GPL-3.0.txt). CrossPoint states the same for its own firmware
from the release after 2.0.0
(https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader/pull/4064).

CrossPoint also notes an open question: whether the LPPL terms of some
hyphenation patterns (section 5) are compatible with the GPL for the combined
image. CrossMono ships the same patterns.


2. Source for a release
-----------------------

The source of a CrossMono release is its tag in
https://github.com/nandanito/crossmono, with the FreeInk SDK submodule, and
the platform and libraries that PlatformIO downloads at the versions named in
platformio.ini. The source archive that GitHub offers for a tag does not
contain the submodule. To get the full source and rebuild a release:

    git clone --recursive https://github.com/nandanito/crossmono.git
    cd crossmono
    git checkout <tag>
    git submodule update --init --recursive
    pio run -e papermono-gh_release

A release candidate (a tag such as 0.1.0-rc.1) is built with
"CROSSMONO_RC=1 pio run -e papermono-gh_release_rc". The build tools are
described in docs/contributing/getting-started.md. The scripts/ folder holds
the build-time patches that CrossPoint applies to some libraries
(scripts/patch_*.py, scripts/sdfat_patches/, scripts/jpegdec_patches/).

Each release has the asset crossmono-<version>-LICENSE.txt, written by
scripts/mono/release_license.py after the release build. It names the tag, the
source commit and the FreeInk SDK commit, and where PlatformIO downloaded each
library from. It holds LICENSE, this file, and the full text of each licence
named here: the texts of the downloaded libraries, the texts in licenses/, and
the texts in the source files and the SDK. Keep it with copies of the firmware.

The folder licenses/ holds licence texts and notices that CrossPoint collected
(GPL-3.0, LGPL-2.1, LGPL-3.0, Apache-2.0, LPPL-1.3c, the ESP-IDF component
notices, the hyphenation pattern notices, the copied-code notices and the font
notices). They are copied unchanged from CrossPoint's develop branch (commit
136c2655), before the CrossPoint release that brings them.


